240
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:26,311
LITTLE GIRL
MISSES HER CAT.

241
00:11:26,311 --> 00:11:30,482
CRAZY LADY THINKS HER
MOTHER IS IN A CAT.

242
00:11:30,482 --> 00:11:32,150
OKAY. YOU KNOW WHAT?

243
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,692
I HAVE TO HAVE DINNER
WITH MY SON.

244
00:11:33,692 --> 00:11:36,655
CAN I TRUST WHEN YOU SEE PHOEBE,
YOU WILL TELL HER?

245
00:11:36,655 --> 00:11:38,031
YES.
YEAH.

246
00:11:38,031 --> 00:11:39,740
THANK YOU.

247
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:44,538
I HATE IT
WHEN ROSS IS RIGHT.

248
00:11:44,538 --> 00:11:46,164
HE IS RIGHT, ISN'T HE?

249
00:11:46,164 --> 00:11:48,082
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT? I THINK
THIS MIGHT BE ONE OF THE TIMES

250
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,083
WHEN HE'S WRONG.

251
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:50,084
YOU THINK?
YOU THINK?

252
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:51,378
OH, NO. HE'S RIGHT.

253
00:11:56,007 --> 00:11:57,050
HI.
HI.

254
00:11:57,050 --> 00:11:58,510
HEY.

255
00:12:00,178 --> 00:12:01,471
UH, PHEEBS...

256
00:12:01,471 --> 00:12:02,721
ABOUT YOUR MOM...

257
00:12:02,721 --> 00:12:03,931
YEAH?

258
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:09,229
HOW'S THAT GOING?

259
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:10,647
SO GREAT.

260
00:12:10,647 --> 00:12:12,482
OH, WE TOOK A NAP
TOGETHER TODAY.

261
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:15,026
MY MOM FELL ASLEEP
ON MY TUMMY AND PURRED.

262
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:18,405
THAT'S SO SWEET.

263
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:23,326
I'M GOING TO GET
SOME COFFEE.

264
00:12:23,326 --> 00:12:24,619
OKAY.

265
00:12:29,040 --> 00:12:30,958
HUH? WHAT'D YOU SAY, JOE?

266
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,751
I'LL BE RIGHT THERE.

267
00:12:36,172 --> 00:12:37,507
PHEEBS...

268
00:12:37,507 --> 00:12:39,509
I JUST FEEL SO... OH...

269
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:41,844
ALL RIGHT, ALREADY. GEEZ!
I'M COMING ALREADY.

270
00:12:46,807 --> 00:12:48,435
( knock at door )

271
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:49,810
NOT YET, NOT YET,
NOT YET, NOT YET

272
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,688
NOT YET, NOT YET,
NOT YET!

273
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,153
HELLO, CHIP.
HEY, RACH, HOW YOU DOING?

274
00:12:59,153 --> 00:13:00,655
I'M GREAT. I'M GREAT.

275
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,282
GOT A GREAT JOB
AT BLOOMINGDALE'S

276
00:13:02,282 --> 00:13:04,075
I HAVE WONDERFUL FRIENDS

277
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:06,035
AND EVEN THOUGH I'M NOT
SEEING ANYONE RIGHT NOW

278
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:08,871
I'VE REALLY NEVER FELT
BETTER ABOUT MYSELF.

279
00:13:10,998 --> 00:13:12,791
SO, UH, MONICA READY YET?

280
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,922
SHE'LL BE OUT
IN A SECOND.

281
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:21,551
SO, CHIP, HOW'S,
UM, AMY WELSH?

282
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:22,677
AMY WELSH?

283
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:24,803
WOW. I HAVEN'T SEEN HER SINCE...

284
00:13:27,098 --> 00:13:28,683
SO... MONICA ABOUT READY?

285
00:13:31,018 --> 00:13:33,688
THIS IS THE UNIT
FOR YOU, MY FRIEND--

286
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:36,941
STURDY CONSTRUCTION,
TONS OF STORAGE COMPARTMENTS

287
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:39,277
SOME BIG ENOUGH
TO FIT A GROWN MAN.

288
00:13:39,277 --> 00:13:41,195
WHAT?

289
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:44,031
OH, YEAH. I GOT
IN THERE MYSELF ONCE.

290
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:46,409
MY ROOMMATE BET ME
FIVE BUCKS THAT I COULDN'T

291
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:48,161
AND THEN HE STUCK A BOARD
THROUGH THE HANDLES

292
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:51,205
AND LOCKED ME IN-- YEAH.

293
00:13:51,205 --> 00:13:54,417
IT WAS FUNNY TILL I STARTED
FEELING LIKE I WAS IN A COFFIN.

294
00:13:56,002 --> 00:13:57,128
NO, YOU...

295
00:13:57,128 --> 00:13:58,171
YOU CAN'T FIT
IN THAT THING.

296
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,506
THAT'S NOT DEEP ENOUGH.

297
00:13:59,506 --> 00:14:00,799
OH, YEAH?

298
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,969
IF I CAN'T

299
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:07,597
I'LL KNOCK FIVE BUCKS
OFF THE PRICE OF THE UNIT.

300
00:14:07,597 --> 00:14:09,015
YOU HAVE YOURSELF
A DEAL.

301
00:14:09,015 --> 00:14:09,974
OKAY.

302
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,648
SEE? I TOLD YOU.

303
00:14:19,734 --> 00:14:23,029
SOMETIMES I COME IN HERE
JUST TO GET AWAY FROM IT.

304
00:14:25,031 --> 00:14:26,991
HEY, A NICKEL!

305
00:14:31,454 --> 00:14:32,789
HERE WE ARE.

306
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:34,957
OH, MY GOD,
YOU STILL HAVE THE CHIPPER.

307
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:36,376
THE WHAT?

308
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,919
THAT'S WHAT WE USED
TO CALL YOUR MOTORCYCLE

309
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:40,755
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

310
00:14:40,755 --> 00:14:42,549
YOU KNOW, A MOTORCYCLE'S
A CHOPPER

311
00:14:42,549 --> 00:14:44,759
AND YOU'RE CHIP.

312
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:46,553
NEVER MIND.

313
00:14:46,553 --> 00:14:48,929
NO. I THINK IT'S CUTE.

314
00:14:53,184 --> 00:14:54,644
WOW.

315
00:14:54,644 --> 00:14:56,730
A LIPPER FROM THE CHIPPER.

316
00:14:58,857 --> 00:15:01,067
SO, YOU STILL IN TOUCH WITH
ANYONE FROM HIGH SCHOOL?

317
00:15:01,067 --> 00:15:04,111
UM, THERE'S RACHEL,
AND, UM...

318
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:06,489
I THINK THAT'S IT.
HOW ABOUT YOU?

319
00:15:06,489 --> 00:15:09,283
OH, YEAH, I STILL HANG
WITH SIMMONS AND ZANA

320
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:11,745
AND I SEE SPINDLER A LOT
AND LEVINE AND KELLY

321
00:15:11,745 --> 00:15:14,038
AND I RUN INTO GOLDIE
FROM TIME TO TIME.

322
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:16,666
STICK, BROWN,
ZOLKOV, McGUIRE

323
00:15:16,666 --> 00:15:19,126
J.T., BEARDSLEY...

324
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:20,712
IS THAT ALL?

325
00:15:20,712 --> 00:15:21,880
YOU KNOW, AFTER HIGH SCHOOL

326
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:25,550
YOU JUST KIND OF LOSE TOUCH.

327
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:27,260
OH, YEAH, I RAN
INTO RICHARD DORFMAN.

328
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:28,720
OH, HOW IS HE?
NOT SO GOOD.

329
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:32,348
ME AND SIMMONS
GAVE HIM A WEDGIE.

330
00:15:32,348 --> 00:15:34,225
ISN'T HE AN ARCHITECT NOW?

331
00:15:34,225 --> 00:15:37,270
YEAH, THEY STILL
WEAR UNDERWEAR.

332
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:50,575
OH, MY GOD!

333
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:53,912
WHAT?!

334
00:15:56,539 --> 00:15:58,332
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

335
00:15:58,332 --> 00:15:59,584
YEAH.

336
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:02,837
WHAT HAPPENED?

337
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:07,216
OH, MAN! HE PROMISED
HE WOULDN'T TAKE THE CHAIRS.

338
00:16:07,216 --> 00:16:09,803
WHAT THE HELL HAPPENED?
HOW WERE YOU LOCKED IN THERE?

339
00:16:09,803 --> 00:16:12,513
WHERE THE HELL'S
ALL OF OUR STUFF?

340
00:16:12,513 --> 00:16:14,265
WELL, THIS GUY CAME BY
TO LOOK AT THE UNIT

341
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,100
AND HE SAID HE DIDN'T
THINK IT WAS BIG ENOUGH

342
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:18,352
TO FIT A GROWN MAN.

343
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:21,021
SO, YOU GOT IN
VOLUNTARILY?

344
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,858
I WAS TRYING
TO MAKE A SALE.

345
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,944
OH, MAN. IF I EVER
RUN INTO THAT GUY AGAIN,

346
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:27,361
YOU KNOW WHAT
I'M GOING TO DO?

347
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,362
BEND OVER?!

348
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:33,868
( chuckling )

349
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:37,330
AND THEN ZANA
JUST LET ONE RIP!

350
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:44,545
NOT THAT I DON'T ENJOY
TALKING ABOUT PEOPLE

351
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:48,007
WE WENT TO HIGH SCHOOL
WITH, 'CAUSE I DO

352
00:16:48,007 --> 00:16:50,468
BUT MAYBE WE COULD TALK
ABOUT SOMETHING ELSE.

353
00:16:50,468 --> 00:16:52,971
LIKE YOU.
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHERE YOU WORK.

354
00:16:52,971 --> 00:16:55,556
YOU KNOW WHERE I WORK.
I DO?

355
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:57,934
THE MOVIE THEATER.
YOU USED TO COME IN
ALL THE TIME.

356
00:16:59,602 --> 00:17:01,145
YOU STILL WORK
AT THE MULTIPLEX?

357
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:04,482
LIKE I'D GIVE UP THAT JOB.

358
00:17:04,482 --> 00:17:07,193
FREE POPCORN AND CANDY
ANYTIME I WANT?

359
00:17:07,193 --> 00:17:08,736
I CAN GET YOU FREE POSTERS
FOR YOUR ROOM.

360
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:10,029
THANKS. I'M SET.

361
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:13,825
DO YOU STILL LIVE
WITH YOUR PARENTS?

362
00:17:13,825 --> 00:17:15,284
YEAH, BUT I CAN STAY OUT
AS LATE AS I WANT.

363
00:17:20,707 --> 00:17:22,291
WOW. THEY REALLY
GOT YOU GUYS--

364
00:17:22,291 --> 00:17:24,585
YOUR TV, THE CHAIRS.

365
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:27,588
YEAH, YOUR MICROWAVE,
THE STEREO...

366
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:31,133
OH, MAN, HE TOOK
THE FIVE OF SPADES!

367
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,844
OH, NO, NO. HERE IT IS.

368
00:17:35,889 --> 00:17:37,348
OH, MY GOD.
WHAT HAPPENED?

369
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:39,559
OH, UM, JOEY WAS BORN

370
00:17:39,559 --> 00:17:42,102
AND THEN 28 YEARS LATER,
I WAS ROBBED.

371
00:17:46,106 --> 00:17:48,108
SO HOW WAS YOUR DATE?

372
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:50,277
WELL, YOU KNOW HOW I
ALWAYS WANTED TO GO OUT

373
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,654
WITH CHIP MATTHEWS
IN HIGH SCHOOL?

374
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:53,907
WELL, TONIGHT,
I ACTUALLY WENT OUT

375
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:56,492
WITH CHIP MATTHEWS
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

376
00:17:56,492 --> 00:17:58,494
OH, HONEY, I'M SORRY.

377
00:17:58,494 --> 00:18:01,414
NO, IT'S OKAY. NOT ONLY DID I
GET TO GO OUT WITH CHIP MATTHEWS

378
00:18:01,414 --> 00:18:03,583
I GOT TO DUMP
CHIP MATTHEWS.

379
00:18:03,583 --> 00:18:05,251
OH, THAT'S SO GREAT.

380
00:18:05,251 --> 00:18:07,921
I KNOW.

381
00:18:07,921 --> 00:18:09,380
HEY.

382
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:11,591
SO, UH, WHAT DID THE
INSURANCE COMPANY SAY?

383
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:13,968
OH, THEY SAID,
"YOU DON'T HAVE INSURANCE HERE

384
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:15,344
SO STOP CALLING US."

385
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,017
YOU DIDN'T TELL HER?

386
00:18:24,938 --> 00:18:26,105
OKAY, FINE.

387
00:18:27,314 --> 00:18:28,315
PHEEBS.

388
00:18:28,315 --> 00:18:30,192
YEAH, HI.
HI.

389
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,403
LISTEN, UH...

390
00:18:32,403 --> 00:18:35,949
THIS CAT BELONGS
TO A LITTLE GIRL.

391
00:18:35,949 --> 00:18:39,243
ALL RIGHT? THERE ARE FLYERS
ALL OVER THE PLACE.

392
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:41,746
I'M SORRY, SWEETIE.

393
00:18:41,746 --> 00:18:45,959
HEY, WE CAN TAKE HER BACK
WITH YOU IF YOU WANT.

394
00:18:45,959 --> 00:18:48,628
OH. HM-MMM.

395
00:18:48,628 --> 00:18:52,548
BUT YOU KNOW,
SHE CHOSE TO FIND ME.

396
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,968
I MEAN, I HAVE TO RESPECT
HER DECISION, RIGHT?

397
00:18:56,719 --> 00:18:59,346
IT'S A GOOD CALL.
RIGHT.

398
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:02,058
NO, NO! HEY!
ENOUGH IS ENOUGH!

399
00:19:02,058 --> 00:19:04,268
LOOK, I AM SORRY
THAT YOU FEEL GUILTY

400
00:19:04,268 --> 00:19:06,312
OR WHATEVER ABOUT SPENDING
TIME WITH YOUR NEW MOM

401
00:19:06,312 --> 00:19:08,355
BUT THIS IS NOT
YOUR OLD MOM.

402
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:10,024
THIS IS A CAT, OKAY?

403
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,901
JULIO THE CAT.

404
00:19:13,193 --> 00:19:14,821
NOT MOM. CAT.

405
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,329
OKAY.

406
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:27,541
ROSS, HOW MANY PARENTS
HAVE YOU LOST?

407
00:19:27,541 --> 00:19:29,043
NONE.

408
00:19:29,043 --> 00:19:30,336
THEN YOU DON'T KNOW
WHAT IT FEELS LIKE

409
00:19:30,336 --> 00:19:31,629
WHEN ONE OF THEM
COMES BACK

410
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:32,797
DO YOU?

411
00:19:37,217 --> 00:19:39,553
I BELIEVE
THIS IS MY MOTHER.

412
00:19:39,553 --> 00:19:42,181
EVEN IF I'M WRONG,
WHO CARES?

413
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,933
JUST BE A FRIEND, OKAY?

414
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:45,726
BE SUPPORTIVE.

415
00:19:49,187 --> 00:19:51,398
I'M SORRY.

416
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,942
OKAY.

417
00:19:54,527 --> 00:19:56,570
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO SAY.

418
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:02,493
YOU COULD SAY YOU'RE
SORRY TO HER MOM.

419
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:12,211
I THINK SHE
WOULD LIKE THAT.

420
00:20:22,722 --> 00:20:25,641
COME HERE, HERE,
COME HERE, COME HERE.

421
00:20:27,977 --> 00:20:29,896
MRS. BUFFAY?

422
00:20:32,690 --> 00:20:34,525
SORRY ABOUT
WHAT I SAID.

423
00:20:34,525 --> 00:20:37,987
UM, IT WAS--
IT WAS INSENSITIVE

424
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:41,448
OF ME TO SAY THAT
YOU WERE JUST A CAT...

425
00:20:43,576 --> 00:20:45,745
WHEN CLEARLY YOU ARE ALSO

426
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:49,123
THE REINCARNATED SPIRIT...

427
00:20:49,123 --> 00:20:50,583
OF MY FRIEND'S MOTHER.

428
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:55,880
THANK YOU.

429
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:57,757
WE BOTH FORGIVE YOU.

430
00:20:59,550 --> 00:21:01,552
HONEY, WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO DO ABOUT THE LITTLE GIRL?

431
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:04,304
YEAH. OKAY, LISTEN...

432
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:06,807
UM, MOM, I HOPE YOU KNOW

433
00:21:06,807 --> 00:21:09,143
THAT YOU STILL MEAN
A LOT TO ME

434
00:21:09,143 --> 00:21:11,812
AND YOU'RE WELCOME
TO COME BACK ANYTIME.

435
00:21:11,812 --> 00:21:15,315
PHEEBS, IF SHE COULD
COME BACK AS A COUCH

436
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:17,443
WE'D REALLY
APPRECIATE IT.

437
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:21,030
COME ON, MOM, I'M GOING
TO TAKE YOU HOME.

438
00:21:21,030 --> 00:21:22,782
I'LL GO WITH YOU.
ME, TOO.

439
00:21:24,366 --> 00:21:27,327
OH, YOU KNOW, I GOT
AN EXTRA FUTON.

440
00:21:27,327 --> 00:21:29,247
DUDE, YOU DON'T
HAVE TO BRAG!

441
00:21:29,247 --> 00:21:31,331
WE GOT NOTHING HERE!

